":450,"estimated_tokens_delta":100,"uuid":"24411ad0-bf63-4d4a-8b7e-65877fc21729","session_id":"81108090-7b99-4e85-927c-60fb69eb3061"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcyrEXACjxUcPpYmsQucQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23799,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23799},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81108090-7b99-4e85-927c-60fb69eb3061","uuid":"02309f24-f339-4265-883f-6213605d2607","request_id":"req_011CcyrEVEcwV2TkH4DwAa1j"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcyrEXACjxUcPpYmsQucQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a plan. I don't have your codebase in view, so this assumes a fairly standard setup — tell me if any assumption is off.\n\n## Plan\n\n- **Deps & config**: `jsonwebtoken`, `bcrypt` (or `argon2`) for password hashing. Put `JWT_SECRET` (or an RS256 key pair), token TTLs in env — never hardcode. Fail fast at boot if the secret is missing.\n- **User store & signup/login**: hash passwords on registration; on login verify hash and issue tokens. Never log or return the hash.\n- **Token issuance**: short-lived **access token** (~15 min) + longer **refresh token** (~7 days) with a `/refresh` endpoint. Sign minimal claims (`sub`, `role`, `exp`) — no PII.\n- **Auth middleware**: verify signature + expiry, attach `req.user`, return 401 on failure. Apply it to protected routes; keep auth routes public.\n- **Refresh & revocation**: store refresh tokens server-side (DB/Redis) so logout and compromise can revoke them — plain JWTs alone can't be invalidated before expiry.\n- **Hardening**: rate-limit login/refresh, generic \"invalid credentials\" errors (no user enumeration), HTTPS-only, validate input.\n\n## Two decisions that change the code\n\n1. **Token transport** — `Authorization: Bearer` header (simple, good for pure APIs/mobile) vs **httpOnly cookies** (safer against XSS, but needs CSRF protection). I'd default to Bearer for an API; cookies if a browser SPA on the same site is the main client.\n2. **Signing algorithm** — **HS256** (one shared secret, simplest) vs **RS256** (private/public keypair, better if other services must verify tokens without the signing secret). I'd default to HS256 unless you have multiple services.\n\nWant me to proceed with the defaults (Bearer + HS256 + access/refresh), or adjust first? Also — what's your user store (Postgres/Prisma, Mongo, something else)? That's the one detail that meaningfully shapes the code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23799,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23799},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81108090-7b99-4e85-927c-60fb69eb3061","uuid":"234be27f-4751-47c0-9d6d-8b597d75ebee","request_id":"req_011CcyrEVEcwV2TkH4DwAa1j"},{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":20376,"duration_api_ms":21395,"ttft_ms":9513,"ttft_stream_ms":2169,"time_to_request_ms":275,"num_turns":1,"result":"Here's a plan. I don't have your codebase in view, so this assumes a fairly standard setup — tell me if any assumption is off.\n\n## Plan\n\n- **Deps & config**: `jsonwebtoken`, `bcrypt` (or `argon2`) for password hashing. Put `JWT_SECRET` (or an RS256 key pair), token TTLs in env — never hardcode. Fail fast at boot if the secret is missing.\n- **User store & signup/login**: hash passwords on registration; on login verify hash and issue tokens. Never log or return the hash.\n- **Token issuance**: short-lived **access token** (~15 min) + longer **refresh token** (~7 days) with a `/refresh` endpoint. Sign minimal claims (`sub`, `role`, `exp`) — no PII.\n- **Auth middleware**: verify signature + expiry, attach `req.user`, return 401 on failure. Apply it to protected routes; keep auth routes public.\n- **Refresh & revocation**: store refresh tokens server-side (DB/Redis) so logout and compromise can revoke them — plain JWTs alone can't be invalidated before expiry.\n- **Hardening**: rate-limit login/refresh, generic \"invalid credentials\" errors (no user enumeration), HTTPS-only, validate input.\n\n## Two decisions that change the code\n\n1. **Token transport** — `Authorization: Bearer` header (simple, good for pure APIs/mobile) vs **httpOnly cookies** (safer against XSS, but needs CSRF protection). I'd default to Bearer for an API; cookies if a browser SPA on the same site is the main client.\n2. **Signing algorithm** — **HS256** (one shared secret, simplest) vs **RS256** (private/public keypair, better if other services must verify tokens without the signing secret). I'd default to HS256 unless you have multiple services.\n\nWant me to proceed with the defaults (Bearer + HS256 + access/refresh), or adjust first? Also — what's your user store (Postgres/Prisma, Mongo, something else)? That's the one detail that meaningfully shapes the code.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"81108090-7b99-4e85-927c-60fb69eb3061","total_cost_usd":0.268635,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23799,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1201,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1201,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_c